commit c67f9ea62fd863721237e7d2298b2aff6a8e9faa
Author: Seth Ford <sethford@studio.local>
Date:   Sat May 16 10:26:06 2026 -0400

    feat(sprint-7): judgment-fidelity NLL seam shipped dormant (US-7.6)
    
    Adds hu_ml_nll_compute_fn_t function-pointer seam alongside the
    existing lexical-surface fidelity scorer. Per sprint 7 decision D3,
    the seam ships DORMANT: production default returns
    HU_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED and the new `check-lora-ab.sh --judgment` path
    emits a visible non-pass SKIP line so US-7.5's nightly cron cannot
    silently treat the inactive gate as a green light. Follow-on
    US-7.6.1 (deferred to sprint 8) will wire a real NLL backend.
    
    Backward compat: hu_ml_fidelity_score_baseline signature unchanged
    (pinned by compile-only test). Header changes are strictly additive.
    
    What landed:
      - include/human/ml/fidelity.h: typedef hu_ml_nll_compute_fn_t,
        set_nll_compute_fn setter, holdout types,
        hu_ml_fidelity_score_judgment, default_holdout_path
      - src/ml/fidelity.c: production default returns NOT_SUPPORTED;
        JSONL holdout loader; scorer accumulates mean/min/max NLL
      - src/ml/cli.c: --judgment flag on `human ml fidelity-status`
        emits judgment_ppl / judgment_ppl_status / scored / skipped
      - scripts/check-lora-ab.sh: --judgment flag; visible SKIP line
        when no NLL backend is registered
      - tests/fixtures/judgment_fidelity_holdout.jsonl: 12 synthetic
        rows, ASCII-only, zero PII
      - tests/fixtures/judgment_fidelity_holdout_malformed.jsonl:
        loader-robustness fixture
      - tests/test_ml_fidelity_judgment.c: 9 tests covering AC-7.6.1
        through AC-7.6.4 + edge cases; mock NLL seam, never loads real
        weights
      - tests/test_check_lora_ab_judgment.sh: AC-7.6.5 — asserts SKIP
        line is emitted and parseable as non-pass

